{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CWPgjB2McR1wth5w9ASLhe","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"liquid lithium density correlation g/cm3 temperature Davison 1968 or IAEA lithium thermophysical properties\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ntrs.nasa.gov\",\"url\":\"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19680018893/downloads/19680018893.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"LITHIUM (Li)\",\"url\":\"https://qedfusion.org/LIB/PROPS/PANOS/li.html\"},{\"title\":\"repo.qst.go.jp\",\"url\":\"https://repo.qst.go.jp/records/47902\"},{\"title\":\"Operational conditions:\",\"url\":\"https://www.chemeo.com/mid/22-277-a/Choline-chloride_Urea_lithium-chloride\"},{\"title\":\"repo.qst.go.jp\",\"url\":\"https://repo.qst.go.jp/records/47902/export/json\"},{\"title\":\"wulixb.iphy.ac.cn\",\"url\":\"https://wulixb.iphy.ac.cn/article/doi/10.7498/aps.55.76\"},{\"title\":\"Contents - Index\",\"url\":\"https://fchartsoftware.com/ees/libr_help/hs400.htm\"},{\"title\":\"densite et temperature de cristallisation d une solution aqueuse de 22391\",\"url\":\"https://iifiir.org/fr/fridoc/densite-et-temperature-de-cristallisation-d-une-solution-aqueuse-de-22391\"},{\"title\":\"Full version\",\"url\":\"https://m.mathnet.ru/eng/tvt703\"},{\"title\":\"elogim.com\",\"url\":\"https://springerlink.bibliotecabuap.elogim.com/content/pdf/10.1361/105497198770341761.pdf\"}]\n\nI ran one search. It did not turn up the Davison 1968 report or an IAEA lithium property table, but it found two useful leads.\n\n- **Empirical density correlation (qedfusion.org):** This page gives a fit for liquid lithium density in g/cm³ as a cubic polynomial in a shifted temperature, with the shift set at 271.7 and the temperature in °C. The published value of 0.534 g/cm³ at 20 °C agrees with the fit. The page does not name its original source, so I can't attribute it to Davison or IAEA. Check the source before relying on the coefficients.\n- **NASA 1968 report (ntrs.nasa.gov):** This is a 1968 NASA study that fit lithium property data from a literature review as functions of temperature, using both experimental data and theory. It extrapolates properties to about 1600 K and reports density in kg/m³. It is the closest match to the 1968 timeframe you mentioned, though I did not confirm that it is the Davison work.\n\nI found no IAEA lithium thermophysical property document in these results. Searching for the Davison report by title or for the IAEA liquid lithium property handbook directly would be the next step.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a3ee98b-7002-4283-82d0-8dda5402a44f","uuid":"1067ed9c-b9de-4bec-bbd2-9dd522d935ab","timestamp":"2026-11-01T03:14:05.012Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"liquid lithium density correlation g/cm3 temperature Davison 1968 or IAEA lithium thermophysical properties","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01CPitTzJhT226hv5i998vSK","content":[{"title":"ntrs.nasa.gov","url":"https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19680018893/downloads/19680018893.pdf"},{"title":"LITHIUM (Li)","url":"https://qedfusion.org/LIB/PROPS/PANOS/li.html"},{"title":"repo.qst.go.jp","url":"https://repo.qst.go.jp/records/47902"},{"title":"Operational conditions:","url":"https://www.chemeo.com/mid/22-277-a/Choline-chloride_Urea_lithium-chloride"},{"title":"repo.qst.go.jp","url":"https://repo.qst.go.jp/records/47902/export/json"},{"title":"wulixb.iphy.ac.cn","url":"https://wulixb.iphy.ac.cn/article/doi/10.7498/aps.55.76"},{"title":"Contents - Index","url":"https://fchartsoftware.com/ees/libr_help/hs400.htm"},{"title":"densite et temperature de cristallisation d une solution aqueuse de 22391","url":"https://iifiir.org/fr/fridoc/densite-et-temperature-de-cristallisation-d-une-solution-aqueuse-de-22391"},{"title":"Full version","url":"https://m.mathnet.ru/eng/tvt703"},{"title":"elogim.com","url":"https://springerlink.bibliotecabuap.elogim.com/content